  "notes": "Actual individual broken Tsar Bell anddisplayed fragment:flared thick bronze shell,closed upper shoulder andhollow underside,real missing front wedge withoriginal irregular closed fracture edges,recessed dark safety grille,separate thick curved fragment leaning beside thepedestal,open cast crown handles,onion-shaped cap andplain cross. Raised bands andoriginal abstract oval/rosette/cartouche relief replace portraits,saints andinscriptions. Circular light-stone pedestal andburied support included. Surrounding paving,tower,churches,palaces andall native context remain independent;no navigable interior orcopied artwork. Two actually inspected ordinary whole/oblique photographs andcurrentstandard PMTiles. WNW broken-side orientation isapproximate with25-degree uncertainty;the photograph camera/context supplies the sign,not surveyed geometry. Original simplified fracture andabstract ornament arean interpretation,not an exactscan orportrait/text reproduction. Exact pedestal/fragment thresholds,interiors,current safety-grille fitting inventory,physical timings andnumerical LOD errors remainunmeasured.",
